  <rect x="0.5" y="1" width="39" height="39" rx="19.5" stroke="#FF5570"/>
  <path d="M20.0048 21.6654L24.9495 16.7218L26.3623 18.1342L20.0048 24.4902L13.6473 18.1342L15.0601 16.7218L20.0048 21.6654Z" fill="#FF5570"/>
  </svg></div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq_text-wrapper">
                  <p class="tab_faq-text">The customer display screen includes a filter by consumption mode: dine-in, in-restaurant, takeout, or delivery. This feature allows you to precisely adapt the display depending on the screen's location. It is particularly useful for differentiating a customer area from an area dedicated to delivery drivers. For example, a screen in the dining room can only display takeout or dine-in orders, while a screen at the entrance or in a dedicated area can be reserved for delivery orders.</p>
                </div>
